class:: StereoCoherence
summary:: Averaged magnitude-squared coherence within a frequency band
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/FFT

description::
Each Hann-windowed frame updates exponentially averaged left/right power and complex cross power. Each bin contributes |P_LR|.squared/(P_LL*P_RR), averaged across the selected band with shared-energy weights 2*sqrt(P_LL*P_RR). This is an averaged spectral coherence estimator following the cross-spectrum definition used in Welch analysis, with exponential averaging in place of a finite segment average. Four frames are required before output; stationarity over averageTime remains necessary.

Uses two private radix-2 FFTs and precomputed Hann windows. frameSize and hop are fixed at construction. CPU is O(frameSize*log(frameSize)) per hop; all storage is allocated before processing. First output is available after frameSize/sampleRate, with coherence held at zero for another three hops; reliable averaging takes approximately averageTime. Frequency selection is quantized to FFT bins. Source for the cross-spectral definition: link::https://www.mathworks.com/help/signal/ref/mscohere.html::.

Vanilla FFT exposes separate spectral frames; this UGen combines two channels and maintains cross-spectral averages.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: left
Left audio-rate input.

argument:: right
Right audio-rate input.

argument:: frameSize
Literal FFT power of two, 256..8192.

argument:: hop
Literal frame fraction, 0.0625..1; default 0.5.

argument:: averageTime
Exponential spectral averaging constant, clipped to 0.01..10 seconds.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included frequency in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included frequency in Hz; zero means Nyquist.

returns::
Coherence from zero through one; silence or no shared energy returns zero.

examples::
Low and high source bands occupy opposite sides, with a small channel delay. The selected band measurement controls a tone's pitch and position.
code::
(
Routine({
    ~mir2Buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var left = LPF.ar(source, 900) + (HPF.ar(source, 1800) * 0.15);
        var right = LPF.ar(source, 900) * 0.15 + HPF.ar(source, 1800);
        var value = StereoCoherence.kr(left, DelayC.ar(right, 0.01, 0.001), minFreq: 100, maxFreq: 2500);
        var control = value;
        var tone = Pan2.ar(SinOsc.ar(control.linexp(0, 1, 180, 1100), 0, 0.035), control * 2 - 1);
        ([left, right] * 0.2 + tone) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.4)
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
Stop and release the buffer:
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
~mir2Buffer.free;
)
::

